From 610fe92e5ad7b5b343789c30009a554443d0bf98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retrorepair <joelwhybrow@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:15:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] input: GunCal starts with the calibration screen, like a
 console game's own GunCon calibration

With a calibration already saved, the GunCal core came up on the plain monitor page and the PS1-style calibration (the yellow screen, "aim at
the cross and shoot") was only reached by holding the trigger for 3 seconds, which nothing on screen says before it is done. Loading the core now
starts the calibration at once. A saved one is replaced only when the five shots are accepted, so leaving early keeps it, and the monitor page
is still there after the check page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 input.cpp | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/input.cpp b/input.cpp
index e4c5ae7..74b614a 100644
--- a/input.cpp
+++ b/input.cpp
@@ -2530,10 +2530,13 @@ static void guncal_service(const struct input_event *ev)
 		memset(&f, 0, sizeof(f));
 		guncal_file_name(d, name, sizeof(name));
 		int have = FileLoadConfig(name, v, sizeof(v)) && guncal_fit_from_file(v, &f);
-		guncal_init(&gcal, have ? &f : NULL, cfg.guncal_margin);
+		// Like a console game's own GunCon calibration: loading the core puts the calibration screen up at once, whether or not one was
+		// saved before. A saved one is replaced only when the five shots are accepted (leaving early keeps it), and the monitor page is
+		// still there, after the check page.
+		guncal_init(&gcal, NULL, cfg.guncal_margin);
 		gcal_x = gcal_y = gcal_trig = 0;
 		gcal_on = true;
-		printf("GunCal: %s\n", have ? "loaded the saved calibration" : "no saved calibration, starting the sequence");
+		printf("GunCal: starting the calibration%s\n", have ? " (the saved one is replaced when the five shots are accepted)" : "");
 		guncal_send(true);
 		gcal_refresh = now + 500;
 	}
-- 
